    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17983968/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a898-5f2623b242b9": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - Dept of Academic Quality & Resources | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer - Dept of Academic Quality & Resources Fixed Terms Closing on 23 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 As Singapore's first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is as a polytechnic for all ages, we prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready, and world ready for the transformation of Singapore. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. What you will be working on We are looking for an experienced and hands-on professional to join our FabLab team. In this role, you will develop and deliver applied learning in digital fabrication, electronics, programming and maker education, while supporting the safe, reliable and effective operation of SP FabLab. You will help students and partners translate ideas into functional prototypes through design, making, testing and iteration. Key Responsibilities 1. Curriculum Design & Development Design, implement, and review curriculum that integrates digital fabrication, innovation, and maker education aligned with SP’s Education Model and MOE directions. Lead the development of hands-on, interdisciplinary learning modules to promote applied learning and innovation. 2. Teacher Capacity Building & Professional Development Conduct training and mentoring for teachers within SP and partner schools to strengthen teaching capability in design thinking and digital fabrication. Develop resources, workshops, and frameworks to scale Maker Education across schools. 3. Strategic Leadership & Partnerships Lead and execute the FabLab Strategic & Scaling Plan to position SP as a national hub for Maker Education. Represent SP FabLab in national MOE initiatives, industry collaborations, and international networks (e.g., Fab Academy). 4. Innovation & Research Drive innovation in pedagogy and applied technology integration within curriculum and outreach programs. Undertake research or pilot projects to evaluate impact and improve programme scalability. 5. Programme Quality Assurance Ensure programme alignment with institutional and national quality standards. Establish sustainable systems for student and teacher engagement, evaluation, and progression. What we are looking for Essential Requirements Bachelor’s Degree in Education, Engineering, Design, Technology, or a related field.  At least 5 years of relevant teaching and curriculum development experience, preferably in tertiary or applied learning environments.  Demonstrated experience in curriculum design, project-based learning, and innovation pedagogy.  Proven ability to plan, deliver, and evaluate hands-on, technology-enabled learning experiences.  Strong communication and stakeholder engagement skills to collaborate with schools, MOE, and industry partners. Preferred Requirements Fab Academy Diploma or equivalent certification in Digital Fabrication / Maker Education is a plus.  Experience in leading teacher training, educational innovation projects, or national education initiatives.  Recognized track record in curriculum innovation, STEM/STEAM education, or design thinking integration.  Experience working with national education agencies, research institutions, or international Maker networks.  Curriculum and pedagogy innovation in Digital Fabrication, Design Thinking, and Maker Education.  Integration of technology-enhanced learning and applied innovation into formal and informal education contexts.  Leadership in scaling sustainable education models across schools and institutions. Candidates should be prepared to present a technical portfolio and may be required to complete a teaching demonstration and/or practical technical assessment as part of the selection process. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 23 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17842877/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-a7ff-285c44ae1405": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Cybersecurity)",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Cybersecurity) | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Cybersecurity) Fixed Terms Closing on 23 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic is challenging and meaningful. Not only will he/she has both the knowledge and working experience, he/she must also possess the ability to deconstruct the knowledge and experience, guiding students to reconstruct them as their own knowledge. He/she must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing them, and moulding their characters. There will be opportunities to develop the curriculum, introduce new courses as well as be involved in consultancy and other applied research projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/Institutional strategic initiatives will be an important part of the job too.  Successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful and innovative with initiative and good communication skills. What you will be working on Cybersecurity The appointee must be competent to teach in at least three of the following subjects: Secure Coding Applied Cryptography Industrial Control Systems / OT Security Malware Reverse Engineering Ethical Hacking and Defences Operational Technology Security IOT and Cloud Security Responsibilities:- Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials, and facilitate learning of students (youths and adult learners) Develop and maintain new/existing teaching curriculum.  This includes regular review of existing curriculum and make recommendations on areas of improvements that would enhance students’ learning, performance and employability. Keep current and abreast of trends and developments of Cybersecurity Support the School’ strategic initiatives through involvement in committee work and projects such as process improvement projects, development and management of new courses What we are looking for Requirements:- Minimum 2 years of relevant work experience in either web and application programming, application security/penetration testing, risk & vulnerability assessment, threat management and defence, security operations and incident response with practical hands-on experience or computer/mobile forensics and investigation. Passionate about education and possess strong interest in teaching and mentoring both youths and adult learners. Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team. Good knowledge of both Linux and Windows based environments. Familiar with the various IT security standards and frameworks, IT best practices, IT security compliance and audit standards. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 23 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
