    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/16993196/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a4d3-ae70289b42ad": {
      "title": "Lead (Continuing Education & Training)",
      "description": "Lead (Continuing Education & Training) - School of Computing | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lead (Continuing Education & Training) - School of Computing Fixed Terms Closed Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic and continuing education leader is challenging and meaningful. Beyond having strong educational and industry understanding, the appointee must possess a passion for lifelong learning, workforce upskilling and industry collaboration. The role involves leading Continuing Education & Training (CET) initiatives within the School of Computing, strengthening partnerships with employers and agencies. Successful candidates are expected to be resourceful, collaborative and forward-looking, with strong leadership, communication, stakeholder management and project delivery skills. What you will be working on Continuing Education & Training Leadership and Industry Engagement The appointee will lead and coordinate CET initiatives within the School of Computing, working closely with academic teams, PACE, industry partners, alumni and external agencies to develop relevant programmes, strengthen learner outreach and support Singapore’s continuing education and workforce transformation needs. Responsibilities: Lead and oversee CET functional areas within the School of Computing, including CET planning, programme operations and achievement of school-level CET targets. Drive the development, launch and continuous review of market-responsive CET programmes, including part-time diplomas, specialist diplomas, Work-Study Programmes, SCTP, short courses and modular training. Strengthen industry engagement, plan & execute outreach initiatives and key account management by identifying collaboration opportunities and maintaining effective relationships with industry partners. Contribute to school-level strategic initiatives, including alumni collaboration, industry projects, staff capability development and the growth of new computing-related CET domains. What we are looking for Requirements: Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in continuing education and training, adult learning, programme management, industry engagement, business development, academic administration or related areas. Proven ability to lead projects, coordinate cross-functional teams, manage stakeholders and deliver outcomes within agreed timelines. Self-driven, resourceful and able to work collaboratively across teams and stakeholders. Knowledge of IT, computing or digital transformation areas such as artificial intelligence, data analytics, software development, cloud, cybersecurity, automation or low-code platforms would be a plus. Preferably able to develop content and curriculum in emerging AI areas. Relevant qualification in Computing, Information Technology, Education, Business, Management or related disciplines. Postgraduate qualifications, adult education credentials or relevant professional certifications would be an added advantage. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17912291/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a488-471cc57b02ad": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Architecture)",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Architecture) - School of ABE | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Architecture) - School of ABE Fixed Terms Closed Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. The role of an academic is challenging and meaningful. Not only does he/she need to have domain knowledge and working experience, he/she must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing them and molding their characters. The job offers opportunities for curriculum and pedagogical development, as well as industry engagements in the form of consultancy or applied research. Administrative work related to teaching and school/institutional strategic initiatives will be an important part of the job.  Successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful, innovative and articulate. Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Architecture) The appointee must be competent to teach in the following key areas of the Construction Industry Transformation Map (ITM) and architectural domains at diploma level: •\tIntegrated Digital Delivery (IDD), with a focus on Computational Design and A.I. applications •\tArchitectural Design •\tHistory and Theory of Architecture •\tEnvironmental Science •\tGreen Buildings •\tMaterials and Technology •\tDesign for Manufacturing & Assembly (DfMA) What you will be working on Responsibilities:- Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials, and facilitate learning for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) students with an emphasis on Computational Design, A.I. applications and History and Theory of Architecture. Keep abreast of current developments and trends in the areas of the Construction Industry Transformation Map and/or Architectural domains to develop and maintain relevant and up-to-date teaching curriculum. This includes review of existing curriculum with a view to making recommendations on areas of improvements that would enhance students’ performance, learning & employability. Enhance students’ learning through other activities such as training students for competitions, supervising projects and internships, and leading them on overseas learning program/community service. Collaborate with other staff as well as industry to offer meaningful applied industry projects and consultancy projects.  Support SkillsFuture initiatives in the implementation of Enhanced Internship Programmes, Work Study Programme and CET programmes. What we are looking for Requirements: Possess relevant qualifications and professional certifications in Architecture, with at least 4 years of relevant experience, preferably in Computational Design and AI applications. Demonstrate strong knowledge of Architectural History and Theory from the 1900s onwards. Exhibit a passion for teaching, knowledge-sharing, and mentoring students and adult learners. Demonstrate strong communication and interpersonal skills, and work effectively as a team player. Ability to engage industry partners and contribute to consultancy projects. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. Apply Save About your application process If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
    },
