      "title": "Assistant/ Deputy Manager, Service-Learning",
      "description": "Assistant/ Deputy Manager, Service-Learning - Dept of Student Development | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Assistant/ Deputy Manager, Service-Learning - Dept of Student Development Fixed Terms Closing on 25 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The Department of Student Development (SD) provides all SP students with a positive Polytechnic experience through meaningful out-of-classroom activities that support holistic student development. As an Assistant Manager/Deputy Manager, the appointee will initiate and lead programmes within the Service-Learning portfolio in the Department of Student Development, with the aim of developing students' social responsibility, character, leadership and community engagement through meaningful service-learning experiences. He/she will be supporting the strategic directives for Service-Learning with involvement in programme planning, stakeholder engagement, communications and conducting relevant data analysis for tracking and continuous improvement. The role will also include mentoring/guiding students in Co-Curricular Activities (CCA) club matters. He/she may be required to collaborate with diverse stakeholders to organise SP-wide events that enhance campus vibrancy and participate in departmental committees. What you will be working on a) Design and lead service-learning and sustainability programmes and activities, ensuring objectives are achieved: Coordinate programme execution, logistics and stakeholder engagement Conduct data tracking, analysis and reporting for continuous improvement Manage programme administration, budgets and vendors (where applicable) Support communications and outreach for programmes and initiatives b) Develop and maintain partnerships with diverse stakeholders to lead meaningful service-learning and sustainability programmes and opportunities. c) Mentor and guide students in CCA clubs, including leadership development and administrative support. d) Support departmental administrative processes and perform ad-hoc duties as assigned. What we are looking for Passion for student/youth development. Minimum 2 years’ experience in service-learning, youth development, education or related fields. Strong organisational, administrative and analytical skills. Good interpersonal, communication and stakeholder engagement skills. Self-motivated, proactive and able to work independently as well as collaboratively. Willing to work beyond office hours when required. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 25 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best 