      "title": "Lecturer (AI & Data Science), Sch of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics",
      "description": "Lecturer (AI & Data Science), Sch of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer (AI & Data Science), Sch of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics Fixed Terms Closing in 1  day(s) Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The job of an academic is challenging but meaningful. Not only will s/he have both the knowledge and working experience, s/he must also possess a passion for working with youths and adult learners. There will be opportunities to develop curriculum, introduce new courses as well as be involved in consultancy and applied industry/research projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/ Institutional strategic initiatives will also be an important part of the job. The successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful and innovative with initiative and good communication skills. What you will be working on As a lecturer in the School of Mathematical Sciences & Analytics, you will be primarily responsible for teaching in the domain of Data Science & Artificial Intelligence , with a focus on at least one of the following areas: Artificial Intelligence (AI) Computer Vision (CV) Data Science (DS) Data Analytics (DA) Natural Language Processing (NLP) You will also be expected to teach in at least one complementary area such as Mathematics, Statistics, or Computing. In line with SP's Common Core Curriculum, you will also be expected to teach at least one interdisciplinary module, which may include: Data Fluency Artificial Intelligence & Its Impact Persuasive Communication with Data Storytelling Problem Solving with Creative and Computational Thinking Beyond the classroom, you will play an active role in shaping and evolving the curriculum. This includes: Developing and reviewing course materials and assessments to enhance student learning, performance, and employability Staying current with trends and developments in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Vision, Data Science, Data Analytics, and Natural Language Processing to ensure the curriculum remains relevant and up to date Undertaking project and consultancy work with internal and external stakeholders, applying your expertise in real-world contexts What we are looking for Passionate about education and possess strong interest in teaching and mentoring students Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team Relevant qualification in Mathematics, Statistics, Physics or Engineering Relevant industry experience and/or knowledge of how statistics is applied in different fields such as Data Analytics, Engineering or IT People-oriented individual with strong interpersonal, written and communication skill Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing in 1  day(s). If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
