sis and Management •\tInternational Trade Finance •\tWealth Management What you will be working on Responsibilities: Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials, and facilitate learning for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) students. Keep abreast of current developments and trends in the areas mentioned above to develop and maintain relevant and up-to-date teaching curriculum. This includes review of existing curriculum with a view to making recommendations on areas of improvements that would enhance students’ performance, learning & employability. Enhance students’ learning through other activities such as training students for competitions, supervising projects, and internships, and leading them on overseas learning programme/community service. Identify new partnership opportunities, building industry partnerships, and cultivating industry relationships. Participate in consultancy projects with industry partners to support the transformation of the industry. Collaborate with other staff as well as industry to offer meaningful applied industry projects and consultancy projects. Support IBF / SkillsFuture initiatives in the implementation of Enhanced Internship Programmes and CET programmes. Handle administrative work relating to teaching. What we are looking for Requirements: At least 3 years of relevant working experience across financial institutions such as banks, brokerages, and/or insurance companies. Part-time experience in education would be an added advantage. Strong passion in mentoring students and show genuine concern for their development. A strong team player with good communication skills Proven ability to engage with the industry on Banking/Finance/Analytics/Fintech consultancy projects. Relevant qualifications in Banking/Finance/Analytics/IT or equivalent such as  MFAS/CACS/CFA/CAIA would be an added advantage. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If 