    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/18037155/005056a3-d347-1fe1-aaf8-5a51e15ea2bc": {
      "title": "Systems Analyst",
      "description": "Systems Analyst - Department of Information and Digital Technology Services | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Systems Analyst - Department of Information and Digital Technology Services Fixed Terms Closing on 07 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The appointee will be responsible for managing and delivering enterprise IT applications. The candidate should possess in-depth technical knowledge, project management capabilities. What you will be working on Develop, enhance and maintain new and existing ASP.NET Core, Microsoft 365, mobile, responsive web and DevSecOps enterprise applications in cloud environments such as AWS. Conduct investigations into user-reported incidents and resolve application issues. Manage application servers such as IIS and deploy applications to ensure smooth service operations and availability for all users. Design and develop secure, scalable and user-centric applications following modern software engineering and DevSecOps practices. Manage the full project cycle, including planning, consultation with users and management of external contractors and consultants. Ensure compliance with security and regulatory standards. Provide technical and operational support for existing enterprise applications. Manage external contractors to ensure service management and delivery. What we are looking for Minimum 3 years of hands-on experience in managing projects and delivering enterprise IT systems. Minimum 2 years of hands-on experience in web and mobile application development using C#, ASP.NET Core, iOS, Android, responsive web technologies, Microsoft 365, jQuery, Bootstrap, CSS and HTML. Experience with cloud platforms (such as AWS) and DevSecOps practices will be advantageous. Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team. Self-motivated learner with passion to explore new technologies. Excellent communication and writing skills with an eye of details. Ability to multi-task and prioritize work to meet set targets. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 07 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
