    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/18037125/005056a3-d347-1fe1-aaf8-582f384522bc": {
      "title": "Senior Executive/Assistant Manager-Dept of Technology, Innovation & Enterprise",
      "description": "Senior Executive/Assistant Manager-Dept of Technology, Innovation & Enterprise | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Senior Executive/Assistant Manager-Dept of Technology, Innovation & Enterprise Fixed Terms Closing on 07 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 Singapore Polytechnic is seeking a meticulous and proactive professional to support the governance and management of its research, innovation and commercialisation funding portfolio. The role is suitable for persons who wish to develop themselves in the field of technology innovation, with a keen interest to facilitate and support scientists and innovators to develop and transfer new technologies to companies.  The appointee will coordinate internal and external grants across the project lifecycle, support the TIE Fund Allocation (TIEFA) Committee, monitor project performance and funding utilisation, and work closely with Principal Investigators, Technology Centres and corporate departments. The role also provides exposure to intellectual property, contracts, licensing and commercialisation matters through collaboration with TIE subject-matter experts. What you will be working on Responsibilities • Coordinate assigned internal and external grants from application and award through implementation, completion and post-project follow-up. • Review grant submissions, project amendments, deviation requests, progress reports and final reports for completeness, compliance and timely submission. • Track project milestones, KPIs, budgets, fund utilisation and reporting obligations; follow up with project teams and escalate material risks or delays. • Plan and coordinate TIEFA funding exercises and meetings, including applicant communications, agenda and paper preparation, project presentations, minutes, decisions and follow-up actions. • Advise Principal Investigators and project teams on established grant processes, policies, terms and reporting requirements, and coordinate clarification of non-routine matters with relevant stakeholders. • Maintain accurate project databases, records and audit trails, and prepare portfolio dashboards, management reports and submissions for internal and external stakeholders. • Provide portfolio support to assigned Schools and Technology Centres, including coordination of funding, project, IP, contract, licensing and commercialisation matters with relevant TIE subject-matter experts. • Liaise with Finance, HR, Legal, grant agencies, auditors, industry partners and other stakeholders to support effective project delivery and governance. • Develop and improve grant-management SOPs, templates, checklists, guidance materials and digital records, and support other innovation programmes and initiatives as assigned. What we are looking for Requirements • Relevant qualifications or experience in areas such as Finance, Engineering, Science & Technology, Computer Science, Information Technology or its equivalent. • Preferably 2-4 years of relevant experience in STEM research, research administration, grants, programme or project management, finance, governance, secretariat work or an innovation-related function.  Fresh graduates in STEM or finance fields with prior work experience in science or innovation research are welcome to apply. • Good analytical, writing, organisational and follow-through skills, with confidence in handling project data, budgets, spreadsheets and management reporting. • People-oriented individual with excellent interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills . • Self-driven, independent and ability to work with others as a team • Prior experience in contracts/partnerships agreements, managing grant funded research or innovative projects portfolio will be an advantage. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 07 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17579935/005056a3-d347-1fe1-aaf8-58c289f882bc": {
      "title": "Senior Executive (Finance)",
      "description": "Senior Executive (Finance) – PACE Academy | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Senior Executive (Finance) – PACE Academy Fixed Terms Closing on 07 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 Singapore Polytechnic's Professional and Adult Continuing Education (PACE) Academy is a leading continuing education and training (CET) academy that advocates the pursuit of lifelong learning and skills mastery. We offer a wide range of training programmes for adult learners to enhance their employability, and partner the industry closely in workforce development. Reporting to the Manager or equivalent, the Finance role is part of the PACE Finance team focused on executing finance and accounting operations in PACE Academy. What you will be working on Responsibilities:- Budget and Grant Management Coordinate budget preparation, forecasting and budget review exercises. Monitor budget utilisation, grant balances and funding availability. Process grant claims, disbursements, journals and related financial transactions. Monitor purchase commitments and budget utilisation. Financial Reporting and Reconciliation Prepare financial reports, dashboards and supporting analyses. Assist in variance analysis and management reporting. Perform grant reconciliations and investigate discrepancies. Support year-end closing, accruals and financial reporting activities. Compliance, Audit and Stakeholder Support Support compliance with grant conditions, SP policies and financial regulations. Maintain audit trails and supporting documentation. Support internal and external audits. Liaise with stakeholders on budget, funding and grant-related matters Support process improvement initiatives. What we are looking for Requirements:- Preferably 3 to 5 years of relevant experience in budgeting, grant management, finance operations, management reporting or financial analysis Experience in grant administration, public sector funding, education institutions or government-funded programmes is preferred Experience in audit, compliance or financial governance will be advantageous Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Good understanding of budgeting, forecasting and financial reporting Knowledge of grant administration and compliance requirements Proficiency in advance Microsoft Excel and financial systems such as Workday Strong communication and stakeholder management skills Meticulous, organized and able to manage multiple priorities independently Comfortable working in a fast-paced and dynamic environment, balancing multiple grants, budgets, reporting requirements and ad hoc requests concurrently Strong ability to adapt to changing business needs, funding requirements and operational priorities Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 07 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17883574/005056a3-d347-1fe1-abc3-ca9ab63ba2bd": {
      "title": "Senior Executive (Programme Ops)",
      "description": "Senior Executive (Programme Ops) - PACE | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Senior Executive (Programme Ops) - PACE Fixed Terms Closing on 10 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Singapore Polytechnic's Professional and Adult Continuing Education (PACE) Academy is a leading continuing education and training (CET) academy that advocates the pursuit of lifelong learning and skills mastery. We offer a wide range of training programmes for adult learners to enhance their employability, and partner the industry closely in workforce development. Reporting to the Senior Manager (Short Course), the appointee will support the administration and operations of CET training programmes. What you will be working on Responsibilities:- Administer learner registrations, enrolments, withdrawals and attendance records. Coordinate course logistics, including classrooms, training facilities, learning platforms, and teaching resources. Liaise with academic staff, trainers, vendors, and stakeholders to support smooth course delivery. Coordinate examination preparation and support exam invigilation duties when required. Assist with data collection and reporting for internal reviews, management reporting, and external submission where applicable. Support process improvements, operational coordination, and other CET-related administrative duties as assigned. What we are looking for Requirements:- At least 3-5 years of working experience, preferably in educational programme management or training operations. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications. Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with stakeholders. Strong organisational, time management and multitasking abilities. Adaptable and able to work effectively in a fast-paced environment. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 10 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
