    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17284129/005056a3-d347-1fe1-ac8f-3acd6c2cc2bd": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Human Resource)/Lead",
      "description": "Lecturer (Human Resource)/Lead – School of Business | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer (Human Resource)/Lead – School of Business Fixed Terms Closing on 12 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 Ranked #19 for The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers 2024 & 2025 We are looking for a dynamic and industry-engaged Lecturer/Lead to join the Business Innovation Centre (BIC) within the School of Business. This role supports teaching, industry engagement, and applied learning initiatives in the areas of Human Resource Management, AI Fluency, and Business Transformation. It plays a key role in driving value exchange between the institutions, industry partners, trade associations, and government agencies. Why Join BIC, School of Business? The BIC aims to be the preferred partner of enterprises in organisation’s business transformation journey, by providing solutions to innovate their businesses, enhance productivity, build international connections, and to develop human capital capabilities. The BIC services include diagnosing business capability gaps, designing business capability development solutions and deploying them and follow up with determining if the solution is effective. Key Roles: The Industry Engagement/Partnerships lead is responsible for supporting the Business Innovation Manager in the centre’s industry outreach to forge value-added partnerships and collaborations with industry partners and relevant agencies in the areas of human resource, digitization, and sustainability. There will be opportunities to work on industry-co-created curriculum, introduce new modules/courses on emerging skills to address key trending issues in collaboration with internal and external stakeholders. Administrative work related to marketing and business development and the Centre/Institutional strategic initiatives will be an important part of the job too. Successful candidates will be expected to have a growth mind-set, and be adaptable to the ever-changing industry landscape, both in the domain industry as well as the education sector. He/she is also expected to demonstrate resourcefulness and innovation, with forward-looking initiatives as well as good communication skills. In addition, the appointee must be competent to teach in at least two or more of the following areas: -\tHR-related disciplines such as, but not limited to, Employee Engagement & Relations, L&D, Performance Management, Career Agility, etc -\tHR Technologies and Analytics -\tApplied Generative/Agentic AI for Human Resource workflows What you will be working on Responsibilities: Seek out and business develop possible collaboration opportunities through student projects, staff consultancy and CET workshops. Stay abreast of current developments and trends in HR, Job Redesign, automation, analytics, UXC/DT, artificial intelligence (Generative and Agentic AI), and ESG/sustainability. Execute outreach activities including learning journeys, learning fests, trade shows and exhibitions. Support stakeholder engagement with public and private sectors to foster partnerships and enhance stakeholder relationships. Co-develop internal capabilities to build schools in domain areas such as HR, Job Redesign, Automation and ESG, particularly on the social pillar. Support operations and administrative work such as report preparation, budgeting, contract management, secretariat duties and etc. Any other duties, including cross-divisional projects or events, that may be assigned by the centre. Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials, and facilitate learning for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) students. Keep abreast of current developments and trends in the areas mentioned above to develop and maintain relevant and up-to-date teaching curriculum. This includes review of existing curriculum with a view to making recommendations on areas of improvements that would enhance students’ performance, learning & employability. Support SkillsFuture initiatives and marketing effort for CET programmes. Handle administrative work relating to teaching. What we are looking for Requirements:- More than 3 years of relevant working experience. Experience in Business Development or Consultancy, or Project Management, education and training related fields such as professional development, learning and development, or workforce development, and a track record of establishing partnerships to deliver corporate objectives. Resilient and adaptable to change in a fast-paced environment that requires multi-tasking. A strong team player with excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Strong passion in mentoring both PET and CET students and show genuine concern for their development. Proven ability to engage with the industry on HR, HR AI & Automation and Analytics Enterprise Transformation and Sustainability consultancy projects. Technical proficiency with end-user Generative AI and Agentic AI workflow tools (for example Copilot Studio for agentic workflows, AWS Quick Suite, Workato Agentic workflow, or equivalent in addition to standard use of OpenAI, Gemini, Claude etc). Relevant qualifications in Human Resource, Business/ or equivalent. Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position, you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 12 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/16563908/005056a3-d347-1fe1-a9c8-54fcc7c2e2bb": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Facilities Management",
      "description": "Lecturer, Facilities Management - School of Architecture & the Built Environment | Careers@Gov Expand masthead to find out how to identify an official government website A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Lecturer, Facilities Management - School of Architecture & the Built Environment Fixed Terms Closing on 29 Sep 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. The job of an academic is challenging and meaningful. Not only will he/she have both the knowledge and working experience, he/she must also possess a passion for working with youths, nurturing them and molding their characters. There will be opportunities to develop the curriculum, introduce new courses as well as be involved in consultancy and other applied research projects. Administrative work related to teaching and School/Institutional strategic initiatives will be an important part of the job too.  Successful candidates will be expected to be resourceful and innovative with initiative and good communication skills. Lecturer (Facilities Management) The appointee must be competent to teach diploma and higher levels in the following key areas of Facilities Management: •\tSafety Health & Security •\tStrategic Asset Enhancement •\tDrawing & Visualization •\tData Analytics •\tSmart Facilities Management •\tDigital Twin and BIM Model Application •\tMaintenance of Mechanical, Electrical and Plumbing Services •\tEnergy Management and Audit •\tSustainability & Environmental Management •\tProcurement & Contract Management What you will be working on Responsibilities: - - Conduct lessons, create teaching and assessment materials and mentoring of students - Develop and maintain new or existing teaching curriculum and learning materials for modules stated above - Deploy effective pedagogy to facilitate learning - Undertake projects or consultancy work with both internal and external stakeholders, especially in the areas of Smart Facilities Management What we are looking for Requirements: - - Relevant qualifications in related Built Environment disciplines - Relevant work experience in Facilities Management, preferably with experience in the planning of preventive, routine, and predictive maintenance of building systems. - Have experience and in-depth knowledge in building systems integration and optimisation and digital technologies/smart solutions for facilities management. - Passionate about education and possess strong interest in teaching and mentoring students - Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team - People-oriented individual with strong interpersonal, written and communication skills - Candidates with the following will have an added advantage: Registered workplace safety and health officer Certified Green Mark Professional (GMP) Certified Fire Safety Manager Successful candidate will be offered a 2-year contract in the first instance. If you are shortlisted for the position(s), you should hear from us within 30 days of the closing date of the advertisement. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 29 Sep 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by © 2026 Open Government Products"
    },
    "https://jobs.careers.gov.sg/jobs/hrp/17708276/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-aca8-678ea321340b": {
      "title": "Manager (Industry Development)",
      "description": "Manager (Industry Development) - Centre of Excellence in Maritime Safety (CEMS) | Careers@Gov A Singapore Government Agency Website How to identify Official website links end with .gov.sg Government agencies communicate via .gov.sg websites (e.g. go.gov.sg/open). Trusted websites Secure websites use HTTPS Look for a lock ( ) or https:// as an added precaution. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites. Singapore Public Service Log in All Open Positions / Singapore Polytechnic Singapore Polytechnic Manager (Industry Development) - Centre of Excellence in Maritime Safety (CEMS) Fixed Terms Closing on 14 Oct 2026 Apply Save What the role is Plaque of Commendation (Gold) – NTUC May Day Awards 2026 Most Positive Workplace Collaboration Award – Singapore International Chamber of Commerce (SICC) Awards 2025 The Straits Times Singapore’s Best Employers for 2024, 2025 & 2026 The role of a Business Development manager at CEMS is both challenging and deeply rewarding. We are seeking individuals who not only possess comprehensive relevant knowledge and practical experience in the maritime industry but also demonstrate good communication and teamwork skills. As an industry development manager, you will play a pivotal role in shaping the Centre’s activities in line with the Maritime Technology & Research Roadmap 2026.  This position involves shaping and executing the Centre's industry engagement, research ecosystem development, and commercialisation strategy. The incumbent will serve as the primary interface between CEMS and its external stakeholders including industry partners, research institutions, institutes of higher learning, funding agencies, and international collaborators while ensuring the effective governance, project management, and business development functions of the Centre are delivered to the highest standard. What you will be working on Responsibilities: Design, develop, and implement a comprehensive framework for industry development, engagement, and outreach. Establish systematic processes for identifying, approaching, and sustaining meaningful relationships with maritime industry stakeholders including shipowners, port operators, maritime service providers, classification societies, and technology companies. Drive initiatives that translate research outcomes into practical industry applications, ensuring CEMS remains relevant, responsive, and valuable to the industry it serves. Lead the building and nurturing of a robust research ecosystem by forging strategic partnerships with industry partners, research institutes, and institutes of higher learning. Identify collaborative research opportunities, facilitate joint project development, and position CEMS as the natural convening body for maritime safety research in Singapore. Serve as the primary conduit between CEMS and its key external stakeholders and funding agencies, with particular focus on the Singapore Maritime Institute and other relevant government bodies. What we are looking for Requirements: At least 4-8 years of relevant working experience. Self-driven, independent, and possess readiness to work as a team. Ability to work in a fast-paced changing environment. People-oriented individual with good interpersonal, written, and communication skills. Strong research literacy, with the ability to critically evaluate evidence, synthesize findings from multiple sources If you meet the above requirements and are interested in this exciting opportunity, please apply with your CV and cover letter. Apply Save About your application process This job is closing on 14 Oct 2026. If you do not hear from us within 4 weeks of the job ad closing date, we seek your understanding that it is likely that we are not moving forward with your application for this role. We thank you for your interest and would like to assure you that this does not affect your other job applications with the Public Service. We encourage you to explore and apply for other roles within Singapore Polytechnic or the wider Public Service. About Singapore Polytechnic As Singapore’s first polytechnic, Singapore Polytechnic (SP) prides ourselves in providing the best learning experience for our students in pre-employment and continuing adult education. The mission of SP is to prepare our learners to be life ready, work ready and world ready. Our vision is to be a caring community of inspired learners committed to serving with mastery. Learn more about Singapore Polytechnic Careers@Gov Singapore Get support Contact us Report vulnerability Terms of use Privacy policy Built by ©2026 Open Government Products"
    }
